3 0 obj
<</Parent 69 0 R/Next 4 0 R/Prev 2 0 R/Title(XI. Hast thou reason? I have. Why then makest thou not use of it? For if thy reason do her part, what more canst thou require?)/Dest 1362 0 R>>
endobj
4 0 obj
<</Parent 69 0 R/Next 5 0 R/Prev 3 0 R/Title(XIV. Not as though thou hadst thousands of years to live. Death hangs over thee: whilst yet thou livest, whilst thou mayest, be good.)/Dest 1363 0 R>>
endobj
5 0 obj
<</Parent 69 0 R/Next 6 0 R/Prev 4 0 R/Title(XXXIV. What art thou, that better and divine part excepted, but as Epictetus said well, a wretched soul, appointed to carry a carcass up and down?)/Dest 1364 0 R>>
endobj
6 0 obj
<</Parent 69 0 R/Next 7 0 R/Prev 5 0 R/Title(II. How easy a thing is it for a man to put off from him all turbulent adventitious imaginations, and presently to be in perfect rest and tranquillity!)/Dest 1365 0 R>>
endobj
